  <string name="network_title">Network</string>
  <string name="network_default_route">Default Route</string>
  <string name="network_default_route_footer">Used by every part of the app set to “Follow Default”. Addresses in your tailnet always go through Tailscale while it is on, whatever the route.</string>
  <string name="network_default_route_covers">The app’s own requests use it too: update checks, skill downloads, voice, weather and images in chats. A provider’s model list, usage and sign-in follow that provider’s route. Mirror speed tests always connect directly, to measure this network itself.</string>
  <string name="network_tailscale">Tailscale</string>
  <string name="network_tailscale_footer">Runs inside Minis, without a VPN profile: only Minis\'s own connections can reach your tailnet, and only while Minis is running. “Use Subnet Routes” lets addresses that other devices share (such as a home network) go through Tailscale.</string>
