  <string name="network_exit_node_none">None</string>
  <string name="network_exit_node_dns">Exit Node DNS</string>
  <string name="network_exit_node_fail_closed">Block Shell Traffic If Unreachable</string>
  <string name="network_exit_node_privacy_footer">Exit Node DNS: the shell looks names up through the exit node too. Off: it asks this device’s own DNS server, which sees the names and your real network, but DNS that only works on this device (a VPN app’s, a company’s) keeps working. Tailnet names always resolve through Tailscale.\nBlock Shell Traffic If Unreachable: a shell connection that cannot go through Tailscale fails instead of going out directly from your real address.</string>
